{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q016_pdb_1acc_domain_split","answer":"SCOP 1.75 treated 1acc chain A as one whole-chain domain, d1acca_ (SUNID 43828), classified as f.11.1.1: class f “Membrane and cell surface proteins and peptides,” with Anthrax protective antigen fold f.11, superfamily f.11.1, and family f.11.1.1. This definition remained through SCOPe 2.03. Beginning with SCOPe 2.04, and still in current release 2.08, it was replaced by two domains: d1acca2 (SUNID 238522), A:14-225, classified in all-beta class b, fold b.179 “Anthrax protective antigen N-terminal-like,” PA14-like superfamily b.179.1, PA14 family b.179.1.1; and d1acca1 (SUNID 238521), A:226-735, classified in class f, fold f.60 “Anthrax protective antigen C-terminal-like,” superfamily f.60.1, family f.60.1.1. Residues 1-13 of the 735-residue SEQRES chain are outside the newer SCOPe domain definitions.

The change shows that the former whole-chain classification conflated two independently classifiable evolutionary modules. The modules occupy different classes, folds, superfamilies, and families; therefore, their juxtaposition in one toxin chain does not make them one homologous unit. It also illustrates that curated domain boundaries and classifications can change as broader structural and evolutionary relationships become apparent.

Homology searches should consequently be domain-aware: search A:14-225 and A:226-735 separately with local sequence/profile and structural methods, assess alignment coverage against the relevant domain, and choose representatives or modeling templates independently for the two regions. A match confined to one region must not be transferred to the other region or treated as evidence for whole-chain homology, identical architecture, or shared function. A same-family match is the strongest close relationship here, and a same-superfamily assignment supports probable common ancestry; sharing only a fold or class is structural similarity, not sufficient evidence of homology. The obsolete whole-chain d1acca_ should therefore not be used as a single evolutionary representative or template for both newer domains.","evidence_used":["Pretrained model knowledge (interpretation of SCOP family, superfamily, fold, and class levels; domain-aware homology-search limits)","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info — /api/v1/; /api/v1/releases/current","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry — /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.03/pdb/1acc/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1acc/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_chain — /api/v1/releases/1.75/chains/1accA; /api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1accA","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_; /api/v1/releases/1.75/sids/d1acca_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca1/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1acca2/parents"]}]}
